    {
        "id": "sp-comment-overview",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "sp-tab-5308214e",
        "name": "OVERVIEW\n--------\nThis flow talks Sparkplug B to infused_modbus's `client` (--data-representation-layer mqtt). Start it with:\n  cargo run -p client -- ignored device.toml tcp://<plc> --data-representation-layer mqtt --mqtt-group-id MyPlant --mqtt-edge-node-id Line1\n\nclient's embedded broker listens on 0.0.0.0:1883 by default, reachable here as 127.0.0.1:1883 because this container runs with --network host.\n\nTopic shape: spBv1.0/<group>/<message-type>/<edge-node>/[<device>]\nNBIRTH/DBIRTH = the data's self-description (name/type/alias per metric), published once at connect. NDATA/DDATA = changed values. NCMD/DCMD = commands going the other way (what the two flows below send).\n\nPITFALL - broker deviceGroup/eonName fields (in the config node below): only used by the 'mqtt sparkplug device' node type (Node-RED simulating ITS OWN device). Left blank here on purpose - setting them makes this broker node auto-publish its own synthetic birth ('Sparkplug Devices/Node-Red'), easy to mistake for a real device in the debug output.\n\nPITFALL - every flow redeploy drops and re-establishes the MQTT connection, which takes a few seconds (sometimes with retry backoff). Expect a brief gap right after clicking Deploy.",
        "info": "",
        "x": 150,
        "y": 40,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "sp-in-dcf40caa",
        "type": "mqtt sparkplug in",
        "z": "sp-tab-5308214e",
        "name": "every Sparkplug message",
        "topic": "spBv1.0/#",
        "qos": "0",
        "broker": "sp-broker-d1e66f9a",
