    {
        "id": "rd-comment-overview",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "rd-tab",
        "name": "OVERVIEW\n--------\nRun examples/rolling_door's Modbus server, then infused_modbus's `client` against it:\n  cargo run -p rolling_door_server\n  cargo run -p client -- ignored examples/rolling_door/device-description.toml tcp://127.0.0.1:15502 --data-representation-layer mqtt --mqtt-broker 127.0.0.1:1883 --mqtt-group-id NodeRedTest --mqtt-edge-node-id ClaudeClient\n\nOpen the dashboard at http://localhost:1880/dashboard/rolling-door once both are running.\n\nPITFALL - GROUP_ID/EDGE_NODE_ID are hardcoded in the function nodes below (same as the other tab's pitfall) - edit them there to match whatever --mqtt-group-id/--mqtt-edge-node-id you actually used. The device name (RollingDoor) is fixed - it comes from device-description.toml's [[machines]] name and doesn't need editing.\n\nPITFALL - the status widgets only populate once client's first DBIRTH arrives (or DDATA afterward for values that change) - if you deployed this flow after client already started, click 'Request Rebirth' to get a fresh snapshot of the current state instead of restarting client.",
        "info": "",
        "x": 150,
        "y": 40,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "rd-sub-in",
        "type": "mqtt sparkplug in",
        "z": "rd-tab",
